    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add more spec_urls; set some standard_tracks to false (APIs A-E)]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27671</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27671"/>
        <updated>2025-09-29T11:30:38.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This is a bit of a test PR to see if we could add spec_urls everywhere (especially for behavioral sub features).<br>
Some things came up where we should probably agree on spec_url consistency for a few common sub features:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>worker_support</li>
<li>iterable sub features (forEach, keys, values, iterator, etc)</li>
<li>secure_context_required<br>
I decided to use the spec_url for the interface itself, happy to hear other thoughts.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Also, I think when a sub aspect of e.g. a method is described then it is okay to link to the same spec section as the method. So, basically the sub feature gets the same spec_url as the parent feature.</p>
<p dir="auto">I marked standard_track false for a few things: CSSPrimitiveValue, CSSValue, CSSValueList, DOMError, FeaturePolicy. Doesn't look like these will be going anywhere.</p>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #27456.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3279237470" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27456" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27456/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27456">#27456</a>.</p>]]></content>
